300
00:12:59.440 --> 00:13:03.560
You just posted you won a giant trophy for reading the most books in a year.

301
00:13:03.840 --> 00:13:05.140
Yes, this is correct.

302
00:13:05.600 --> 00:13:07.620
So your book club gave you a trophy?

303
00:13:07.840 --> 00:13:08.580
Like, how did it work?

304
00:13:08.580 --> 00:13:13.200
So I've been in this book club for maybe five years, and it's a competitive book reading

305
00:13:13.200 --> 00:13:13.660
club.

306
00:13:14.000 --> 00:13:14.400
Competitive?

307
00:13:15.820 --> 00:13:21.040
It's like, I'll show you the spreadsheet, but it's like based on what you read, how many

308
00:13:21.040 --> 00:13:22.760
like pages it is, the genre.

309
00:13:23.000 --> 00:13:24.340
You get a certain amount of points.

310
00:13:24.560 --> 00:13:27.700
And it like encourages diverse reading, which is really cool.

311
00:13:27.900 --> 00:13:32.260
Like, I've read a lot of books from different countries, and like, they make sure you're reading

312
00:13:32.260 --> 00:13:34.720
a lot of women and stuff like that, which is really great.

313
00:13:35.140 --> 00:13:35.420
Yeah.

314
00:13:35.600 --> 00:13:38.320
And then last year, I was like, I really want to win this thing.

315
00:13:38.580 --> 00:13:43.840
And I was neck and neck with another reader, and I ended up winning, which was very cool.

316
00:13:43.980 --> 00:13:45.660
But also, I felt crazy.

317
00:13:46.320 --> 00:13:48.960
How many books did you read to win this title?

318
00:13:49.160 --> 00:13:52.000
So I read over 66 books last year.

319
00:13:52.280 --> 00:13:52.760
Wow.

320
00:13:53.000 --> 00:13:54.560
